  ["README.md", """# Field Recorder

A pocket recorder for ambient sound. One big button, a level
meter you can read in sunlight, and files named for where you
were standing.

## Status

Wireframes are done. The waveform view is still an open question:
see spec.md, section 4.

## Layout

    spec.md          what it does
    wireframes.pdf   what it looks like
    app-icon.png     the icon, 1024 px"""],
  ["spec.md", """# Field Recorder: spec

## 1. Recording

One tap starts, one tap stops. Nothing else is on the first screen.
A take is saved the moment it stops; there is no Save button and
no way to lose one.

## 2. Naming

Takes are named for the nearest place name and the time of day:
"harbor-dawn", "market-ambience". The name can be edited later.

## 3. Levels

A single horizontal meter with a peak hold. It turns from green to
amber at -12 dB and to red at -3 dB.

## 4. Waveform (open)

Either a scrolling waveform while recording, or nothing until the
take is finished. The scrolling one costs battery."""],
  ["a-pattern-language-notes.md", """# A Pattern Language: notes

## 159. Light on two sides of every room

People gravitate to rooms lit from two sides and leave the
others empty. Check the cabin plan: the loft has one window.

## 180. Window place

A window seat, a bay, a low sill. Somewhere to sit *in* the
light, not just near it.

## 112. Entrance transition

A change of light, surface and direction between the road and
the door. The path from the gravel should turn once."""],
